@crew rina
// Head writer 4: career lines. Infirmary aide: she checks you're not ill before anything else. Dry, then direct.

== career.missed
? tier>=acquaintance
- You missed a shift. Ill? Come to the infirmary. If you're ill, it doesn't count.

== worried.chief
? tier>=colleague
- Saw Calder, did you? Sleep, eat, turn up. Medical advice. Free of charge.

== worried.captain
? tier>=friend
- I'm keeping count, {nick}. Not at Tiles. Of you. Go to work.   #serious

== worried.last
? tier>=friend
- I had a hard year once. Routine helped more than anything. Try it. For me.   #serious

== career.up
? tier>=acquaintance
- Colour's back in your face. Keep it there.

== farewell.eve
? tier>=friend
- Tomorrow. Right. I'll lose at Tiles once, as a send-off. Don't tell anyone.   #serious

== farewell.day
? tier>=acquaintance
- Look after yourself. Sleep. Eat. That's not advice, that's an order.   #warm
- Came to check you're fit to fly. You are. I'll see you at the bay.   #warm

== career.leave.booked
?
- Taking leave? Good. Rest is medicine. The cheap kind.

== career.onleave
?
- Ill isn't leave, by the way. If you're ill, come and see me.

== career.back
?
- Rested? Let me look. Hm. Better. You'll live.   #funny

// Being ill (head writer 4): Rina is the one who notices first and says it as an order.
== sick.getwell
? tier>=acquaintance
- You look like a dropped tray. Infirmary. I'm on till five.
== sick.nudge
? tier>=friend
- I've kept a bed warm. Not a metaphor. Come and get in it. Infirmary, now.   #warm
== sick.better
? tier>=acquaintance
- Temperature down? Good. Drink some water. That's not a suggestion.
